INT. SHARK TUNNEL - CLOSED AQUARIUM - NIGHT

A glass tube through a vast dark tank. Sharks slide overhead like slow thoughts. Blue light ripples on the floor.

VIVEK SHARMA (40s, crew leader, wetsuit under a janitor's coverall) crouches at a service panel with a flashlight in his teeth. LORNA BISHOP (30s, safecracker, headset, earring) leans on the rail, studying a tablet. BAPTISTE LAROCHE (50s, driver, cardigan) watches the sharks with real concern. SUNNY OKAFOR (20s, rookie, backpack of gear) stands frozen near the exit.

VIVEK
(muttering)
Come on, come on.

LORNA
Sunny, the east door.

SUNNY
Which one's east?

BAPTISTE
The one with the hammerhead.

SUNNY
They all have a hammerhead!

LORNA
(into headset)
Vivek, thirty seconds on the guard.

VIVEK
(around the flashlight)
I know.

BAPTISTE
That one is looking at me.

SUNNY
Sharks don't look.

BAPTISTE
That one does.

LORNA
Everybody, listen. Panel opens in five, four--

VIVEK
Three--

SUNNY
Wait, wait, which door--

BAPTISTE
Left! The left one!

The panel pops. Vivek pulls out a thin steel case and snaps it shut. Lorna is already running. Sunny sprints after her, backpack bouncing.

The alarm begins to whoop. The sharks scatter, a gray bloom in blue.

BAPTISTE (CONT'D)
(to himself)
I told them. I told them about the sharks.
